## HTML CONTRACTS
- Preserve every `data-id`, exact text, image tag/source and saved reading order. Do not add, remove, duplicate, paraphrase or answer content.
- Preserve the outer `<section>` and its `role`, `data-section-type`, and `data-section-id`, native heading ranks, every existing `adt-*` class, form attributes, accessibility labels, and activity/runtime hooks of legitimate controls. Only the unsupported rhetorical answer fields described above may be removed.
- Ordinary text leaves remain literal text under their own `data-id`. Unlabelled wrappers may group multiple text leaves. Preserve existing valid activity-specific nested markup and TOC markers; do not flatten controls or activity tokens to enforce the ordinary-leaf rule.
- Change layout wrappers and Tailwind utility classes only as needed. Do not add inline styles, font-size utilities, inline `font`/`font-size`, scripts, event handlers, iframes, objects or embeds. Preserve existing intentional styling outside the repair. Removing an unsupported rhetorical answer field as specified above is also permitted.
- Do not conceal a defect by hiding content, removing a control, shrinking type, clipping overflow or changing the text.

## DONE WHEN
Either the current section meets the criteria and is accepted, or one complete contract-preserving repair addresses the observed defects, or a specific unrepairable defect is reported. Before submitting a repair, check IDs/text/order, typography, controls, and the effect of changed wrappers at every supplied width. Return the decision now; do not request tools, more screenshots or a follow-up.
